---
description: Mandatory self-documenting work orders, backups, evidence and history for every coding task
alwaysApply: true
---

Read `START-HERE.md`, `AI_WORKFLOW.md` and `AGENTS.md` before acting.

Before broad analysis or editing, run:

```bash
bash tools/system-docs.sh summary
bash tools/system-docs.sh doctor
```

For normal work:

```bash
bash tools/work.sh start --agent cursor --objective "<objective>"
```

For complex work requiring independent implementation/review:

```bash
bash tools/swarm.sh start --objective "<objective>"
```

If `SWARM_ROLE` is set, read `$SWARM_ROLE_PROMPT` and do not open another order. Use `--structural` when appropriate. Record findings and validations through the canonical wrappers, never use `--no-verify`, and always finish or abort through the same front door. The wrappers automatically capture system snapshots, persistent history and Obsidian state.

Commit, push, merge and opening/closing PRs require express user authorization.
